        "original_id": "d644ad1e-a580-5f2b-b7c6-09d154c11f21",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: William Bainbridge, John Adams, Abigail Adams\n- Organizations: United States Navy, Royal Navy\n- Products: USS Bainbridge (DDG-96), USS Constitution, HMS Java\n- Events: War of 1812\n- Roles: Commodore, president, diarist, correspondent\n\nFacts:\n- William Bainbridge was born on May 7, 1774, and died on July 27, 1833.\n- William Bainbridge was a Commodore in the United States Navy.\n- During his long career in the early United States Navy, William Bainbridge served under six presidents beginning with John Adams.\n- John Adams was a dedicated diarist and correspondent, especially with his wife and closest advisor Abigail Adams.\n- In the War of 1812, William Bainbridge commanded USS Constitution and captured HMS Java, a 38-gun fifth-rate frigate of the Royal Navy.\n- USS Bainbridge (DDG-96) is named in honor of Commodore William Bainbridge.",
